# 1. Roadmap rules

## 1.1 Product truth before execution convenience

Each milestone starts from the filmmaker-visible production decision it must preserve, then defines durable authority, historical behavior, failure semantics, and only then downstream execution behavior.

```text
filmmaker decision
    ↓
production authority
    ↓
immutable publication/capture
    ↓
observation/materialization
    ↓
execution
```

No milestone may reverse this direction.

## 1.2 Every milestone must be independently source-gateable

A milestone boundary is valid only when its central product claim can be proven without assuming a later milestone.

Examples:

```text
M11 may prove immutable reusable Production Revision publication
without Composition existing.

M13 may prove that SoloRing remembers an exact reusable world
without final execution of that world being implemented yet.

M14 must prove that the newly captured reusable world reaches execution;
it may not relabel M13's memory-only state as renderability.
```

## 1.3 Design gates close before milestone-plan freeze

A roadmap design gate is not an implementation task hidden inside a milestone.

For each milestone:

```text
open design question
    ↓
focused design decision
    ↓
source-fit against current baseline
    ↓
frozen milestone plan
    ↓
separate implementation authorization
```

If a design gate exposes a substantive architecture contradiction rather than an implementation choice, affected milestone planning stops and the architecture artifact is corrected first.

## 1.4 Historical closure is part of product completion

Current-state success alone never closes a production-authority milestone.

Any new identity that can enter captured history must also have:

```text
immutable capture
captured-graph-only read path
fail-closed missing-history behavior
Exact Rerun isolation
no current/latest substitution
```

before the milestone claims that identity as production-ready.

## 1.5 UI is a projection of the same authority

Each filmmaker-facing surface must consume the same resolver/publication/readiness contracts used by capture and execution. UI behavior never becomes a parallel authority interpretation.

## 1.6 No speculative platform completion

A milestone implements only the abstraction required by its declared product slice.

Examples:

```text
one usable retained representation
    before
universal multi-representation lifecycle

one minimum immutable Performance representation
    before
universal rig/editor architecture

one camera-only candidate adoption route
    before
universal candidate-world ingestion
```

