# 4. Milestone M12 — Composition and Stable Production Occurrences

## 4.1 Filmmaker-facing problem

A reusable chair is not yet a reusable lobby. SoloRing needs to assemble exact Production Revisions into a persistent set and know which occurrence is which.

M12 gives the filmmaker a reusable Composition with durable addressable occurrences.

## 4.2 Roadmap scope

Primary graph nodes:

```text
CO-01
CO-02
CO-03
minimum CO-05
minimum CO-06
```

Minimum product surface:

```text
create Composition working state
add exact Production Revisions
mint durable addressable occurrences
publish immutable Composition Revision
edit one occurrence with explicit scope
publish a later Composition Revision while surviving occurrences retain identity
```

## 4.3 Required pre-plan design gate

**G2 — Composition/occurrence/scope family** must close before M12 plan freeze.

It must decide:

1. How occurrence identities are minted.
2. How one occurrence identity is referenced across Composition Revisions.
3. Which publication changes preserve identity by default.
4. Which operations explicitly change identity.
5. What affected-state diagnostics must exist for remove/replace/split/merge/fork operations.
6. The minimum typed override vocabulary needed for the first slice.
7. How API/UI exposes consequential edit scope without asking unnecessary questions.
8. How published Composition Revision closure pins exact Production Revisions and nested dependencies.

## 4.4 Explicit non-scope

M12 does not yet claim:

```text
instance-bound world state
instance-bound spatial authority
Composition↔Spatial binding
historical Shot capture of the reusable world
production-world rendering
bulk/procedural populations
safe automatic update offering
```

## 4.5 Source-gate proof boundary

M12 closes only when source evidence proves:

- occurrence identity is not a display name, hierarchy path, representation object ID, array position, or filesystem location;
- publishing a new Composition Revision preserves every surviving occurrence identity by default;
- changing a referenced compatible Production Revision does not automatically mint a new occurrence;
- identity-changing operations are explicit and lineage-bearing;
- Shot-local/source-substitution override semantics cannot silently become Composition-global edits;
- ambiguous edit scope is surfaced before consequential mutation;
- historical Composition Revisions remain immutable;
- no Composition transform becomes a competing authority for facts already owned by spatial authority.

## 4.6 Product exit statement

> SoloRing can publish a reusable set assembly whose addressable occurrences remain the same production occurrences across Composition evolution unless the filmmaker explicitly changes their identity.

This is S2 / Bundle B complete.

