# 6. Milestone M14 — World Observation and Execution Enforcement

## 6.1 Filmmaker-facing problem

Remembering the world is not enough. The world must be observed by an executor without re-inventing its identity/state and without silently dropping hard production requirements.

M14 closes the execution boundary for the production world.

## 6.2 Roadmap scope

Primary graph nodes:

```text
OB-01
OB-02
OB-03
EX-01
```

It consumes M13 captured production-world state and the M11/RP-03 publication semantics. M14 must add or select one production-capable retained representation/materialization path under those semantics; that path does not have to be part of the initial M11 consumer scope.

## 6.3 Required pre-plan design gate

**G6 — Observation contract** must close before the main M14 plan freezes.

It must decide:

1. Versioned World Observation specification boundary.
2. How existing specialized observation inputs project into that boundary.
3. Preservation/trust vocabulary, at least enough to distinguish hard, structural, identity/appearance, bounded, and inferable properties.
4. How Shot-level generative freedom is represented without transferring authority to execution.
5. Relationship between observation specification and the existing durable execution specification.
6. How capability negotiation reports unsupported hard requirements before queueing.
7. How observation artifacts are versioned and proven disposable/rebuildable without becoming authority.

The remaining execution-facing portion of **G7** must also close: exact new production-world inputs captured by M13 must project into OB-02 without current-state lookup.

## 6.4 Two-stage implementation structure

M14 should preserve the graph's OB-01/OB-02 distinction.

### M14A — observation/trust contract over existing captured domains

Equivalent to S8:

```text
OB-01 + OB-03 + EX-01
```

This proves the generalized contract and pre-queue failure semantics without claiming reusable-world support yet.

### M14B — production-world observation support

Adds:

```text
OB-02
+ exact M13 captured Production/Composition/Instance/state/binding inputs
+ one production-capable retained representation/materialization path
```

Only M14B may close SHOOT THE WORLD.

## 6.5 Source-gate proof boundary

M14 closes only when source evidence proves:

- observations derive only from immutable captured state for historical execution;
- current resolvers are not consulted by Exact Rerun observation materialization;
- preview/inspection and final execution consume the same captured authority/binding semantics;
- changing observation format/version does not change production identity;
- unsupported hard requirements fail before queueing;
- unknown execution dependency classes fail safe rather than being dropped;
- executor/materializer output cannot write production authority as a side effect;
- one real retained production representation path produces the required structural/identity controls for the declared test workflow;
- the same M13 reusable world can be shot from a new camera without creating a new world identity;
- a lower-control Shot may allow more inference without changing the underlying world authority.

## 6.6 Product exit statement — SHOOT THE WORLD

> **SoloRing can compile an exact captured reusable world into a supported production execution path, preserve declared hard constraints, and reject incompatible execution before expensive work.**

This is S4 / Bundle D complete and closes **SHOOT THE WORLD**.

