# 9. Post-M16 and non-reordering side branches

The following capabilities remain valid and valuable, but the roadmap does not assign them automatic implementation priority before M11–M16 close.

## 9.0 Corrected capability frontier

The post-M16 frontier is no longer allowed to treat lip sync as a self-contained animation/executor feature. The production ordering is:

```text
1. DIALOGUE & VOCAL PERFORMANCE
   • Dialogue Line identity/revisions (A1)
   • speaker + exact wording + language
   • recorded/generated/imported vocal candidates
   • Vocal Performance adoption (A7)
   • immutable retained audio + exact timebase
   • derived word/phoneme/viseme alignment
   • dialogue replacement / compatibility / historical isolation

                ↓

2. PERFORMANCE & ACTING
   • body performance
   • facial performance
   • expression / articulation
   • dialogue-bound lip sync
   • Performance Revisions
   • retargeting / compatibility

                ↓

3. PHYSICAL INTERACTION
   • contact
   • grasping
   • support
   • handling

                ↓

4. SOUND POST / FINISHING
   • Foley / ambience / SFX
   • music
   • final dialogue edit / processing
   • mix / re-recording / mastering
```

An ADR/dialogue edit that materially changes the acting/timing used by animation crosses back into step 1 as a new Vocal Performance candidate; Sound Post cannot silently replace A7 synchronization authority.

## 9.1 Basic advisory QC — RV-03

The graph proves QC is an independent root over already-captured authority.

Recommended entry condition:

```text
SHOOT THE WORLD closed
+ enough real Takes exist to define useful evidence classes
```

Reason to wait:

- QC is more valuable after the world/observation contracts it will inspect are stable;
- early QC risks optimizing evaluation around temporary execution behavior.

First scope should remain advisory. QC evidence never becomes production authority.

## 9.2 Perform the World — Dialogue + Performance program

Performance becomes the next major continuity frontier after persistent world/state workflows, but dialogue-bound facial animation cannot be treated as a self-contained executor feature.

Before the first Performance milestone plan, **G8 — Performance / Dialogue Co-Design** must freeze together:

```text
A1 Dialogue Line revision identity
A7 Vocal Performance revision + retained audio closure
exact audio / Performance / Shot temporal mapping
derived dialogue alignment evidence contract
one minimum body/facial Performance representation
vocal↔facial synchronization + compatibility semantics
Shot capture / historical closure
```

Do not make the program contingent on solving a universal rig/deformation/editor system or full Sound Post. Do not allow it to begin from an arbitrary audio file with no approved vocal-performance identity.

### 9.2.1 M17A — Performance Temporal + Dialogue/Vocal Foundation

Filmmaker-visible exit: an exact semantic line can have one or more candidate vocal takes, one adopted Vocal Performance Revision, retained speech bytes, exact timebase/segment mapping, derived alignment evidence, and explicit replacement/compatibility semantics without facial animation yet.

Primary capability set: `DL-01 + PT-01 + VP-01 + DA-01`.

### 9.2.2 M17B — Body + Facial Performance Revisions

Filmmaker-visible exit: body/facial acting can be created/imported/generated as candidates, reviewed/adopted into immutable Performance Revisions, retargeted only under explicit compatibility, and historically resolved independently of the tool that created it.

Primary capability set: `PF-01` plus the minimum retarget/compatibility surface required by the chosen G8 representation.

### 9.2.3 M17C — Dialogue-Bound Facial Performance + Capture

Filmmaker-visible exit: the adopted facial performance binds an exact Vocal Performance Revision and exact temporal mapping; dialogue analysis remains derived evidence; Shot capture pins the vocal/facial identities and segment; Exact Rerun uses historical closure; one real production execution path proves the approved vocal timing drives the submitted facial controls.

Primary capability set: `PF-03 + PF-02`, consuming M17A/M17B.

## 9.3 Physical relationships — RL-01/RL-02

Relationship authority should follow a real production need such as support, attachment, grounding, containment, or exact contact.

It should not be implemented merely because simulation technology is available.

## 9.4 Candidate-world ingestion — CW-01/CW-02/CW-03

Candidate-world ingestion should begin route-by-route.

Recommended first route:

```text
camera extraction/evidence
    ↓
existing spatial/cinematic review/adoption
```

Object/geometry identity matching should wait for the M11–M13 reusable-production identities it adopts into.

Candidate extraction never bypasses explicit adoption.

---


## 9.5 Targeted correction / delta realization — DX-01

Recommended earliest entry condition:

```text
OB-03 preservation/trust contract exists
+ real accepted Takes expose a bounded correction need
```

Correction produces a new candidate Take from an immutable source Take under explicit change and preservation requirements. It does not mutate the source Take or upstream production authority.

Pre-plan gate: **G9**.

## 9.6 Profile-scoped Production Revision qualification — QL-01/QL-02

Recommended earliest entry condition:

```text
M11 publication capability exists
+ stable immutable realization-profile identity exists
+ one real production criterion needs qualification evidence
```

This branch may be implemented in parallel with M12/M13 if it does not perturb the reusable-world spine. It is not required to close REMEMBER THE WORLD.

Before a production realization profile is declared generally usable for expensive Shot execution, its milestone/source gate may require applicable qualification evidence for the revisions it consumes. That policy decision belongs to the owning realization/observation milestone; no universal `locked` flag is introduced.

Pre-plan gate: **G10**.

## 9.7 Property-scoped reference evidence — VI-01

This is an independent visual-authority extension over existing approved visual identity.

Recommended trigger:

```text
a real production needs multiple references with different property roles
or explicit anti-reference/prohibited-property evidence
```

Pre-plan gate: **G11**.

It should not be implemented as a renderer-specific negative-prompt or reference-bundle feature. The production claim must remain upstream and renderer-independent.


## 9.8 Editorial / Conform / Finishing Co-Design — G12, no milestone assigned

This is a **future design gate**, not a scheduled implementation milestone. Recommended scheduling is after the currently defined Performance priorities unless a concrete delivery need justifies an earlier standalone design exercise. It must not interrupt M15/M16.

Before any authoritative editorial implementation plan freezes, G12 must answer together:

```text
future editorial/edit revision identity
exact approved Take/source-media/stream identity
canonical editorial timebase and exact source-range addressing
trim / order / reuse / first transition semantics
deterministic resolution boundary for defaults, inference, stochastic choices, and meaning-bearing parameters
playback proxy ↔ authoritative source mapping
proof that preview and final realization consume the same resolved editorial meaning
media-preservation classes:
  BYTE_EXACT / STREAM_EXACT / ESSENCE_EXACT / BOUNDARY_REENCODE / FULL_REENCODE
materialization selection:
  preservation conform / composition rendering / mixed strategy
capability negotiation + explicit unsupported/fallback behavior
exact source/output lineage for materialized outputs, including selected materialization mode
interchange/project files as representations, not authority
```

The first future slice should prove **deterministic preservation-safe editorial/materialization foundation** (`S14 / Bundle J`), not a universal NLE, grading suite, Sound Post system, or mastering platform.

LosslessCut, FFmpeg, NLE project formats, and similar tools may inform implementation or serve as downstream operators, but none becomes SoloRing authority by adoption shortcut.

# 10. Deferred reusable-production expansions

Several capabilities are deliberately held until concrete consumers prove their need.

## 10.1 Generalized representation registry — RP-02

Trigger it when at least two real consumer representations require first-class selection, lifecycle, compatibility, or replacement semantics.

Do not build it merely because the architecture permits multiple representations.

## 10.2 General derivation provenance — RP-04

M11 needs enough provenance to distinguish creation history from production identity. A broader derivation graph should expand only when candidate creation/import/repair workflows require it.

## 10.3 Fork / lineage — RP-06

Implement when filmmakers need a reusable object to diverge permanently from its source identity while retaining lineage.

## 10.4 Bulk/procedural instance model — CO-04

Implement only when real production sets require large repeated populations and one repeated element needs promotion into an addressable occurrence.

## 10.5 Generated-detail promotion — RV-02

Implement after Production Object publication exists and a real Take-review workflow needs to promote a generated invention into reusable production authority.

