# 14. Migration and compatibility policy

This roadmap does not freeze migration shapes, but every future milestone plan must obey the following evolution policy.

## 14.1 Do not backfill invented production decisions

If older Projects lack a new reusable-production concept, migration must not invent:

```text
Production Revision approval
Composition occurrence identity
Composition↔Spatial binding
compatibility verdict
persistent consequence
Performance Revision
```

Older data remains valid under its historical schema until the filmmaker creates/adopts the new content.

## 14.2 New historical schemas only when new semantic content exists

A Shot without reusable-production content must not acquire a higher historical schema merely because the software version changed.

## 14.3 Preserve old captured bytes/meaning

Compatibility layers may translate execution views. They may not rewrite historical source identity or bytes to resemble the current model.

## 14.4 Fail closed on missing retained closure

If an old captured Shot says it used a published reusable revision and its required retained closure is missing/corrupt, historical execution fails. It does not substitute the current revision or regenerate an approximation.

