# 17. Post-M16 roadmap program

After M16 and the integrated sequence rerun, the default next program is **PERFORM THE WORLD**, subject to G8 closure and separate milestone authorization:

```text
M17A  Performance Temporal + Dialogue/Vocal Foundation
M17B  Body + Facial Performance Revisions
M17C  Dialogue-Bound Facial Performance + Performance Capture
M18   Physical Interaction / Contact Authority
M19   Performance QC + Targeted Correction
```

This sequence corrects one dependency rather than expanding scope indiscriminately: lip sync requires durable dialogue/vocal authority before facial synchronization. Full soundtrack production is still later. G12 editorial/conform design is a separate downstream branch and does not alter this sequence.

M18 should pull `RL-01/RL-02` from actual contact/grasp/support/handling needs exposed by M17. M19 may combine advisory `RV-03` evidence with `DX-01` targeted correction once real Performance Takes expose bounded correction needs; neither QC nor correction becomes authority.

Other independent roots remain candidates after or alongside this program only when production evidence justifies them:

```text
CW-01/CW-03 camera-only candidate-world route
CW-02 richer object/entity matching
VI-01 property-scoped reference claims
QL-01/QL-02 qualification expansion
RP-02/RP-04/RP-06/CO-04/RV-02 reusable-production expansion
ED-01→ED-05 editorial/conform branch only after G12 scheduling decision
```

