# 19. Roadmap acceptance criteria

This roadmap is internally coherent only if all of the following remain true:

1. M11 can close without M12.
2. M12 can close without claiming persistent world-state/spatial integration.
3. M13 closes historical reusable-world memory before M14 execution expansion.
4. M14 cannot close SHOOT THE WORLD through an observation wrapper that ignores new reusable-world inputs.
5. M15 compatibility cannot rewrite M11–M14 history.
6. M16 consequence adoption remains separate from Take approval.
7. No post-M16 lip-sync milestone may freeze unless G8 has assigned semantic line, approved vocal performance, exact temporal mapping, derived alignment, facial Performance, synchronization, and Sound Post boundaries explicitly.
7. No milestone before M14 is blocked by generalized representation registry, simulation, universal rigging, candidate-world ingestion, or QC.
8. Entity-bound event design remains independent of reusable Production Instances; instance-bound events consume M13 subject support only when needed.
9. G3.1 bindability eligibility is explicitly resolved before M13 plan freeze.
10. Every new historical identity is captured and reproducible from immutable provenance before its milestone claims production completeness.
11. Every milestone has a filmmaker-visible exit claim, not only schema completion.
12. Milestone numbering remains planning order, not implementation authorization.
13. No editorial/conform milestone is assigned until G12 closes; approved Takes remain immutable, proxies remain non-authoritative, and executor syntax cannot become the edit.

